From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:59:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 116/342] arm64: the physical map area replaces the loader's
 reservations

With the physical memory map inside the kernel address space (the
previous commit), the ranges the loader lists for its mappings are
reserved by reserve_boot_loader_ranges() before the area is created
over them, so creating it failed, and the panic for that hung the
boot before any output. Unreserve the map's range first; a failure is
only logged again, since the system runs without the area.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_vm_translation_map.cpp | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_vm_translation_map.cpp b/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_vm_translation_map.cpp
index 3a00f5bd3a..e108432d18 100644
--- a/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_vm_translation_map.cpp
+++ b/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_vm_translation_map.cpp
@@ -96,12 +96,15 @@ arch_vm_translation_map_init_post_area(kernel_args* args)
 {
 	dprintf("arch_vm_translation_map_init_post_area\n");
 
-	// Create an area covering the physical map area.
+	// Create an area covering the physical map area. The loader lists the
+	// map's mappings among the ranges it allocated, which the VM reserved;
+	// the area replaces those reservations.
 	void* address = (void*) KERNEL_PMAP_BASE;
+	vm_unreserve_address_range(VMAddressSpace::KernelID(), address, KERNEL_PMAP_SIZE);
 	area_id area = vm_create_null_area(VMAddressSpace::KernelID(), "physical map area", &address,
 		B_EXACT_ADDRESS, KERNEL_PMAP_SIZE, 0);
 	if (area < 0)
-		panic("arm64: no physical map area: %#" B_PRIx32, area);
+		dprintf("arm64: no physical map area: %#" B_PRIx32 "\n", area);
 
 	if (args->arch_args.uart.kind[0] != 0) {
 		// debug uart is already mapped by the efi loader, in whole pages
